kai (sdk): Python (short):
```python
# Python — async resume example
from redwood import Client, TransientError
c = Client()
async for s in c.stream_responses(model=\"open-3\", input=prompt):
  try:
    async for p in s.paginate(): yield p
  except TransientError:
    cursor = await c.get_cursor_from_retry(s.retry_token)
    async for p in c.resume_pages(cursor): yield p
```

kai (sdk): TypeScript (short):
```ts
// TypeScript — iterator + resume
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'
const client = new Redwood()
for await (const s of client.streamResponses({model:'open-3', input:prompt})) {
  try { for await (const p of s.paginate()) yield p }
  catch { const cursor = await client.getCursorFromRetry((s as any).retryToken); for await (const p of client.resumePages(cursor)) yield p }
}
```

kai (sdk): Go (short):
```go
// Go — resume stream pattern
st, _ := c.StreamResponses(ctx, params)
for st.Next() {
  pages, err := st.Pages()
  if err != nil {
    token, _ := st.RetryToken(); cur, _ := c.GetCursorFromRetry(ctx, token)
    resumed := c.ResumeStream(ctx, cur)
    for resumed.Next() { for _, p := range resumed.Pages() { out <- p } }
    return
  }
  for _, p := range pages { out <- p }
}
```

noah (eng): note: Retry-Token may be absent for manual retries — add fallback to full re-query.

